diff --git a/python/pypto/framework/weight_pack.py b/python/pypto/framework/weight_pack.py
index bda570f2f..12f100e67 100644
--- a/python/pypto/framework/weight_pack.py
+++ b/python/pypto/framework/weight_pack.py
@@ -3,10 +3,18 @@
 J1 stored a plain ``(K, N)`` row-major transpose of the torch weight.  J1.1
 switches the bridge to the W8B **packed/blocked** AVX-512 plane, so the
 payload is no longer a plain matrix: it is the tile layout produced by the
-native ``ptx_avx512_pack_matmul_{f32,bf16}`` kernel (64x64 K/N tiles,
-row-major inside a tile).  The native packer is the single source of truth for
-the layout; this module only describes the self-describing handle format and
-computes sizes.
+native ``ptx_avx512_pack_matmul_{f32,bf16}`` kernel (64x64 K/N tiles).  The
+native packer is the single source of truth for the layout; this module only
+describes the self-describing handle format and computes sizes.
+
+Tile layout (blocks ordered by N block, then K block):
+
+* f32: each block is a plain row-major ``[K_TILE][N_TILE]`` tile;
+* bf16: each block stores VDPBF16PS *k pairs*: for ``pair`` in ``0..31`` and
+  column ``nn``, ``block[pair*128 + 2*nn] = W[n_global, 2*pair]`` and
+  ``block[pair*128 + 2*nn + 1] = W[n_global, 2*pair + 1]`` (so a 32-bit
+  group feeds one bf16 pair into ``_mm512_dpbf16_ps``), with zero padding
+  for out-of-range K/N.
 
 Self-describing handle layout (all little-endian, 32-byte header)::
 
